@6000 = ~Summoning limit has been reached.~
@6001 = ~Elemental Summoning
Level: Quest
Range: 10 yards
Duration: 10 rounds
Casting Time: 1 round
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Drawing power from the environment, this spell summons 2 16HD elementals randomly chosen from earth, air or fire. The elementals stay for 10 rounds and will obey the caster as long as they remain summoned.~

@6002 = ~Defensive Harmony
(Enchantment/Charm)

Level: 4
Sphere: Law
Range: 0
Duration: 6 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 10-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

Defensive Harmony grants affected creatures a defensive bonus by bestowing an enchanted coordination on their attacks and defenses. This allows a group of creatures to act as a single unit for a single battle or encounter. The effect is always centered on the caster, but affects all allies within a 10-ft. radius. Every 6 seconds the caster sends a wave of protective energy, which grants a -2 bonus to AC for 6 seconds to all affected. There are 6 waves, with the last one being sent exactly 30 seconds after the spell is finished casting. The bonuses granted by each wave of energy are considered as combat protections and can be dispelled, however the original spell is undispellable.

Clerics who decided to devote their lives to a single deity get additional benefits from this spell. With every wave all affected party members gain additional physical resistance for 6 seconds (non cumulative) and the caster gets the same bonus for each party member affected (cumulative). This bonus is equal to 2% from level 12 and increases to 3 and 4, at levels 18 and 24 respectively.~

@6003 = ~Weaken Undead~

@6004 = ~Weaken Undead
(Abjuration)

Level: 5
Range: 0 
Duration: 6 rounds
Casting Time: 5 
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

This powerful spell creates waves of positive energy that sweep outward from the caster. These waves disrupt any undead that attempt to attack the caster, reducing the physical damage they deal by 10% and decreasing their chance for critical hit by 5% for 6 seconds. There is one wave per round for the duration of the spell, which renews the effects, but does not stack with itself. All undead are affected with no Saving Throw, this spell bypasses Magic Resistance.~

@6005 = ~Protective Chant~

@6006 = ~Protective Chant
(Abjuration)

Level: 5
Range: 35 ft.
Duration: 1 round
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

This chant provides means of protection against powerful magics. The caster utters only a few words and directs the spell to any point chosen by <PRO_HIMHER>. Every ally in a 15-ft circle receives a short lasting boost to their Magic Damage Resistance. High level priests can make their whole party survive even the dreaded Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting without sustaining any serious damage.

Initially the spell increases Magic Damage Resistance of all affected by 40%, however at 20'th level of the caster this value is increased to 60%~

@6007 = ~Purify Aura~

@6008 = ~Purify Aura
(Generalist)

Level: Quest
Sphere: None
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 0
Area of Effect: Caster
Saving Throw: None 

Experienced Clerics can send a vast amount of energy from the Positive Energy Plane as a single impulse emanating from their bodies and minds. By doing so, they can instantly cleanse their aura at any moment they desire. This however is very taxing to the caster, thus only the most powerful Priests can use this skill in a rapid succession. 

The ability is instantaneous but can only be used once every 3 rounds, this time is reduced to 2 rounds and 1 round at levels 20 and 25 and finally at level 30 it has no cooldown.~

@6009 = ~Heavenly Shield~

@6010 = ~Heavenly Shield
(Conjuration)

Level: 6
Sphere: Law
Range: 0
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Caster
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell the Cleric imbues <PRO_HISHER> shield with divine magic, making it feel lighter in <PRO_HISHER> hand. This allows the caster to use the shield offensively, by searching for openings in enemy's defences and striking with the shield when the time is right. The better the caster's ability to fight using a shield, the greater the benefits of this spell.

Each first hit per round for the next turn deals additional crushing damage if the caster is using a shield. The base value is 2d3 plus additional 2d4 per each point in Sword and Shield style. Each strike is considered as highly magical, even with a non-magical shield, which allows for hitting creatures of magical nature, however spells like Protection from Magical Weapons can block the effects of this spell.~

@6011 = ~Shield Bash~

@6012 = ~Strength of One
(Alteration)

Level: 3
Sphere: Law
Range: 0 
Duration: 1 turn 
Casting Time: 3 
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, party members within the area of effect are given a Strength score of 18/75. If a party member has a Strength score higher than this (either naturally, or through a magical item), then the spell has no effect. The spell lasts for 1 turn, whereupon everyone's Strength returns to normal.~

@6013 = ~Holy Power
(Evocation)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round/level
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Through this spell, the caster imbues <PRO_HIMHER>self with the strength and skill of a Fighter of the same level. The priest's Strength score is set to 18/00 - unless it is higher - <PRO_HISHER> THAC0 becomes that of a Fighter of the same level, and <PRO_HESHE> gains 1 temporary Hit Point per level. This will last for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6014 = ~Cure Light Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 1
Sphere: Healing
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell and laying <PRO_HISHER> hand upon a creature, the priest causes 8 points + 5% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body to be healed. This healing cannot affect creatures without corporeal bodies, nor can it cure wounds of creatures not living or of extraplanar origin.

Curing is permanent only insofar as the creature does not sustain further damage; caused wounds will heal - or can be cured - just as any normal injury.~

@6015 = ~Cure Medium Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 3
Sphere: Healing 
Range: Touch 
Duration: Permanent 
Casting Time: 5 
Area of Effect: 1 creature 
Saving Throw: None 

By casting this spell and laying <PRO_HISHER> hand upon a creature, the priest heals 14 points +15% of wound or other injury damage from the creature's body. This healing cannot affect creatures without corporeal bodies, nor can it cure wounds of creatures not living or of extraplanar origin. Curing is permanent only insofar as the creature does not sustain further damage; caused wounds will heal - or can be cured - just as any normal injury.~

@6016 = ~Cure Serious Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Sphere: Healing 
Range: Touch 
Duration: Permanent 
Casting Time: 7 
Area of Effect: 1 creature 
Saving Throw: None 

This spell is a more potent version of the Cure Light Wounds spell. The priest lays <PRO_HISHER> hand upon a creature and heals 17 points +20% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body. This healing cannot affect noncorporeal, nonliving, or extraplanar creatures.~

@6017 = ~Cure Critical Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 5
Sphere: Healing 
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

The Cure Critical Wounds spell is a very potent version of the Cure Light Wounds spell. The priest lays <PRO_HISHER> hands upon a creature and heals 27 points +25% of damage from wounds or other injuries. The spell does not affect creatures without corporeal bodies, those of extraplanar origin, or those not living.~

@6018 = ~False Dawn (Evocation)
Sphere: Sun
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 12-ft. radius sphere
Saving Throw: None

False dawn calls into existence a bright reddish light, as if a sunrise were occurring, within the area of effect. All vampires, wraiths, spectral undead, mists and shadows within a false dawn suffer 10d4 + 4 points of fire damage. There is no saving throw against this damage. This spell bypasses both Magic Resistance and base Fire Resistance (innate or magical) of the affected creatures.~

@6019 = ~Sunray
(Evocation, Alteration)

Level: 7
Sphere: Sun
Range: 0
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Special

When this spell is cast, it causes a ray of sunlight to beam down upon the caster and everyone within a 15-ft. radius. All creatures within the area of effect take 3d6 points of damage and must save vs. Spell or be blinded for 1 turn. Undead that are hit by the sunray take additional 8d6 damage, which bypasses Magic Resistance and during the impact their base Fire Resistance is reduced by 50% of their current value. Creatures that by some means achieved values of Fire Resistance higher than 100 are completely immune to the effects of this spell.~

@6020 = ~Disrupt Undead (Necromancy)
Level: 7
Range: 15 feet
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: One Undead Creature
Saving Throw: None

By means of this powerful spell, the priest uses <PRO_HISHER> divine powers to disturb the negative forces floating inside an undead creature. The spell bypasses the target's magic resistance (if any) and inflicts a huge amount of damage, which varies depending on the undead type:

- Skeleton Lords (and lesser undead creatures): 10D6 +30
- Skeleton Warlords: 8D6 +24
- Skeleton Grandlords: 6D6 +18
- Liches, Master Vampires and Vampire Lords: 5D6 +15~

@6021 = ~Cause Serious Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Sphere: Healing
Range: Touch
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

This spell is the reverse of Cure Serious Wounds. Instead of healing the creature touched, it causes damage. On a successful touch from the priest, the spell inflicts 17 points of damage upon the target. Each casting of this spell allows for launching two successful strikes, however, <PRO_HESHE> has 1 turn to make the attacks before the spell fizzles. This spell directly affects the nervous system of the touched enemy, bypassing Magic Resistance, though enemies resistant to magical damage will be able to withstand the pain better. Because of the nature of this spell, all non-living creatures, such as undead or constructs are immune to its effects.

The spell covers the priest's hand with magical energies, that provide the following benefits:
- number of attacks per round set to 2,5
- +4 bonus to hit
- bonuses from strength stat are also counted, when determining caster's chance to hit
- caster can direct the energy through a punch, instead of a touch, thus <PRO_HESHE> deals additional crushing damage, based on <PRO_HISHER> strength stat~

@6022 = ~Cause Critical Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 5
Sphere: Healing
Range: Touch
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

This spell is the reverse of Cure Critical Wounds. Instead of healing the creature touched, it causes damage. On a successful touch from the priest, the spell inflicts 27 points of damage upon the target.Each casting of this spell allows for launching two strikes, however, <PRO_HESHE> has 1 turn to make the attack before the spell fizzles. This spell directly affects the nervous system of the touched enemy, bypassing Magic Resistance, though enemies resistant to magical damage will be able to withstand the pain better. Because of the nature of this spell, all non-living creatures, such as undead or constructs are immune to its effects.

The spell covers the priest's hand with magical energies, that provide the following benefits:
- number of attacks per round set to 2,5
- +4 bonus to hit
- bonuses from strength stat are also counted, when determining caster's chance to hit
- caster can direct the energy through a punch, instead of a touch, thus <PRO_HESHE> deals additional crushing damage, based on <PRO_HISHER> strength stat~

@6023 = ~Slay Living
(Necromancy)

Level: 5
Sphere: Combat
Range: Caster
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Upon casting this spell, the priest temporarily gains power to deal more harm to any humanoidal living creature. For 15 rounds he or she gets a +4 damage and +4 thac0 bonus against all humans, elves, halflings and similar creatures of roughly human size. Additionally each melee hit against such creatures has 10% chance to cumulatively curse them, lowering their luck by 1 for 3 rounds.~

@6024 = ~Cursed~

@6025 = ~Harm (Necromancy)
Level: 6
Sphere: Healing
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: Special

This spell creates vast amounts of necromantic energies that swirl around the hand of the caster. The next successful attack (with a +4 bonus to hit) that the priest makes will release these energies, however he only has 3 rounds to make the attack before the spell fizzles. Upon contact with the target, a powerful explosion occurs dealing damage to the target and all enemies around. The effects are as follows:
- the target, who is at the center of this explosion takes 10d6 + 10 magical damage with no save, that ignores magic resistance
- enemies in 5ft. radius from the target take 6d6 +6 magical damage, but can make a saving throw vs spell with a -2 penalty to take only half of the damage
- enemies in 10ft. radius from the target take 4d6 magical damage, but can make a saving throws vs spell to avoid this damage altogether

The energies created by this spell are far more volatile than those from Cause Wounds spells, the caster needs more focus to keep them under his control, which is why this spell grants no bonus attacks per round.~

@6026 = ~Demon Hunt
(Alteration)

Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 15 ft. sphere
Saving Throw: None

This powerful spell was designed specifically to fight against demons from the Abyss. It is centered on the caster, but it affects everyone in the area of 15 feet.
All affected deal additional 3 magical damage against demons. Additionally, each hit done to demons has a 10% chance to increase the demon's chance for Critical Miss by 5% for 3 rounds, this effect is cumulative.~

@6027 = ~Critical miss chance increased~

@6028 = ~Demon Hunt~

@6029 = ~Magical Stone
(Enchantment)

Level: 1
Sphere: Combat
Range: 50 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: Path of projectile
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the priest conjures a small magical stone that flies out at high speed, striking all creatures in its path. The pebble inflicts 1d4+3 points of damage to whomever it hits. Once put into motion, the priest has no control over the stone, and it can harm both allies and enemies.~

@6030 = ~Aid
(Necromancy, Conjuration)

Level: 2
Sphere: Necromantic
Range: Touch
Duration: 1 round + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

The recipient of this spell gains the benefits of a Bless spell (+1 to attack rolls and Saving Throws) and a special bonus of 1d8 additional Hit Points for the duration of the spell. The Aid spell enables the recipient to actually have more Hit Points than <PRO_HISHER> current maximum. The bonus Hit Points are lost first when the recipient takes damage and may not be regained by curative magic.

Example: A 1st-level Fighter has 8 Hit Points, suffers 2 points of damage (8 - 2 = 6), then receives an Aid spell that grants <PRO_HIMHER> 5 additional Hit Points. The Fighter now has 11 Hit Points, 3 of which are temporary. If <PRO_HESHE> is then hit for 7 points of damage, 4 normal Hit Points and all 3 temporary Hit Points are lost. The Fighter then receives a Cure Light Wounds spell that heals 4 points of damage, restoring <PRO_HIMHER> to <PRO_HISHER> original 8 Hit Points.

At levels 1 to 14 this spell targets only 1 creature, from level 15 it works on every ally of the caster in 15 ft. radius.~

@6031 = ~Greater Restoration
(Necromancy)

Level: 7
Sphere: Necromantic
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the life energy level of the recipient is raised. This reverses any previous life energy level drain of the creature by a force or monster. A Greater Restoration spell will also restore the Intelligence score of a creature affected by the Feeblemind spell and negate any form of insanity, such as confusion or berserk. It fully heals the target and cures any diseases or poisons. The casting of this spell is very draining on the priest, and <PRO_HESHE> will suffer a cumulative -2 penalty to luck for the next 3 rounds.~

@6032 = ~Divine Intervention~

@6033 = ~Divine Intervention
(Necromancy)

Level: Quest
Sphere: Necromantic
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Party
Saving Throw: None

This spell connects the caster directly to <PRO_HISHER> god, granting <PRO_HIMHER> and <PRO_HISHER> party a level of healing unlike any other spell. Divine Intervention has similar effect to Greater Restoration, however it is applied to whole party. This spell is extremely taxing to the caster's body and mind, cumulatively lowering <PRO_HISHER> luck by 4 for 5 rounds.~

@6034 = ~Increase Spell Duration I~

@6035 = ~Increase Spell Duration I

High-level priests devout to their god can receive a special blessing from their worshipped deity, which causes the magic of their spells to dissipate more slowly than normal. This blessing extends the base duration of clerical spells by 20%.

This ability does not extend the duration of the following:
-Spells that apply their effects periodically (like True Seeing or Continual Cure)
-Spells that apply different effects to allies and enemies (like Chant)
-Improved versions of spells cast by Cleric kits (like 
 for all Clerics or Righteous Magic for Priest of Tyr)
-Spell-like abilities that are not memorized in Priest spellbook (like Summon Archdeva)~

@6036 = ~Spare the Dying~

@6037 = ~Spare the Dying
(Necromancy)

Level: 7
Sphere: Healing
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the priest strengthens the bond between body and soul of all affected allies. For the next 5 rounds, those allies will be able to withstand one hit per round that would normally kill them, leaving them with 1 HP remaining and immediately healing them for 10HP. Spare the Dying only protects from effects that directly deal damage and does not grant immunity to instant death abilities such as vorpal hits or Power Word: Kill. Additionally, for the duration of this spell, all affected allies won't suffer permanent death from normal damage sources (although they can still be petrified, imprisoned, or frozen solid). The spell and all of its effects are undispeallable.~

@6038 = ~Lethal blow averted~

@6039 = ~Hold Undead
(Necromancy)

Level: 3
Range: 35 ft.
Duration: 3 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 undead creature
Saving Throw: Special

This spell affects the movements of an undead creature, focusing on the lower parts of its body in an attempt to hold it in place and make it more vulnerable to damage. The target's movement speed is reduced by 100%, and its resistance to slashing and crushing damage is decreased by 20% if the creature fails a Saving Throw against the spell at a -2 penalty. A successful Saving Throw will reduce both of these effects by half. Magic Resistance does not protect against this spell. However, it is still treated as a 3rd-level spell, meaning powerful undead creatures such as Liches and Demiliches are not affected.~

@6040 = ~Boon of Lathander
This spell lasts for 1 turn. It gives the caster a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws, +2 to damage and thac0, and +1 extra attack per round.~

@6041 = ~Spiritual Link~

@6042 = ~Spiritual Link
(Alteration)

Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

By opening a direct link between the caster and <PRO_HISHER> god, the caster is able to draw divine energies faster, than normally. This results in <PRO_HIMHER> needing less time to cast spells, which require longer incantations and more focus. The more experience the caster has, the stronger the link and in result, the quicker the casting.

This spell sets casting time of all spells, which have this value higher than 6 to 6. At level 18 this value is reduced to 5, then to 4 and finally to 3 at levels 22 and 26 respectively. Due to direct contact with divine energies, all other means of lowering casting time become useless, however the caster can sever the link at any moment, without wasting <PRO_HISHER> action this round.~

@6043 = ~Break Spiritual Link~

@6044 = ~Lightning Bolt of Talos~

@6045 = ~Lightningbolt of Talos
(Evocation)

Level: Special
Range: 70 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Path of bolt
Saving Throw: 1/2

Upon casting this spell, the priest releases a powerful stroke of electrical energy that inflicts 1d6 points of damage per level of the caster (maximum damage of 10d6) to each creature within its area of effect. A successful Saving Throw vs. Spell reduces this damage to half (round fractions down). If the lightning bolt intersects with a wall, it will bounce until it reaches its full length.

The power and control over this spell increases with the priest's level as follows:
- at levels 1-12 it's treated as a 3rd level spell and affects both enemies and allies
- at levels 13-16 it's treated as a 4th level spell
- at levels 17-20 it's treated as a 5th level spell and only enemies of the caster are affected
- at levels 21 and above it's treated as a 6th level spell~

@6046 = ~SEEKING SWORD: This spell creates a long sword in the Cleric's inventory that only Priests of Helm can use, it stays in <PRO_HISHER> equipment for 1 round per level, up to 20 rounds. The sword can only be used in main hand and to wield the weapon better, the caster must know how to use Long Swords. The sword gets more powerful as the caster gains experience. While the sword is held — and for 2 rounds after it is removed — the Cleric's spellcasting is hampered, reducing the potency of any divine spells cast during that time.

The sword has the following statistics based on levels:
1 - 9: 1-6 + 2 dmg, +2 thaco, 1 APR, priest caster level -1
10-11: 1-6 + 2 dmg, +2 thaco, 1,5 APR, priest caster level -2
12-14: 1-8 + 3 dmg, +3 thaco, 1,5 APR, priest caster level -2
15-19: 1-8 + 3 dmg, +3 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -3, range increased to 2 feet
20-24: 2-4 + 4 dmg, +4 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -4, range increased to 2 feet, +5% chance for critical hit
25-40: 2-6 + 5 dmg, +5 thaco, 2 APR, priest caster level -5, range increased to 2 feet, +10% chance for critical hit.~

@6047 = ~Long Sword Proficiency~

@6048 = ~After many hours of training with Seeking Sword, the priest can gain even more prowess with the weapon. This passive skill gives additional Long Sword Proficiency~

@6049 = ~Divine Favor
This spell grants the caster a +1 bonus to hit and damage rolls every 3 levels of the caster. The spell lasts for 6 rounds.~

@6050 = ~Chaos of Battle
This spell ensures that the next strike from all affected allies will be a critical hit, while the next strike from all affected enemies will be a critical miss. The spell lasts for 1 round. If a creature does not attack during this period, the spell's effect will be wasted on that target.

The area of effect of this spell grows with the caster's level as follows:
At levels 5-10, it affects all creatures within a 5-foot radius.
At levels 11-15, the area is increased to a 10-foot radius.
From level 16 onward, the area is increased to a 15-foot radius.~

@6051 = ~Draw Upon Holy Might (Invocation)
Level: 2
Sphere: Combat
Range: 0
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

The priest calls upon his god to grant him power for a short period. When he does this, his strength, constitution and dexterity all are raised by 1 point for every 3 levels of the caster up till level 12. A third level caster would have his abilities raised by 1, while a 12th level caster would have all his abilities raised by 4.~

@6052 = ~Wisdom of the Ages~

@6053 = ~Wisdom of the Ages
(Divination)

Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: the caster
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the cleric invokes ancient knowledge and insight. This divine inspiration allows the caster to identify items with greater ease and precision, granting him or her additional 30 lore for 5 rounds.~

@6054 = ~Storm of Vengeance

Level: Quest
Range: 50 ft.
Duration: 3 rounds
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Special

Casting this spell causes the earth to shake and the heavens to boil with blood and energy. All enemies of the caster are struck down by acidic rain, earthquakes, and lightning.

All enemies of 8th level or lower are slain instantly. The survivors are struck by acidic, poisonous rain and lightning. The storm lasts for 3 rounds. Each round, the victims suffer 1d6 electrical damage, 1d6 fire damage, and 1d6 acid damage (Save vs. Spell with a -4 penalty for half damage). They also have a chance to be poisoned (Save vs. Death with a -4 penalty negates) in the first round.~

@6055 = ~Champion's Might
(Alteration)

Level: 6
Sphere: Law
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the priest places a divine mark on the target, which lasts for 15 rounds. A moment later a surge of godly energy flows from the priest's body to the nearest party member with said mark active. This energy greatly enhances combat abilities of the target, granting +1 bonus to THAC0 per 5 levels of the caster (up to +4 at level 20) and doubling the number of attacks as if Improved Haste was cast.

The spell applies its effects every 6 seconds to the nearest marked character for its duration and the effects last for the same amount of time. The target has to be in the caster's range for each pulse of the spell, otherwise he'll have to wait for another pulse to get the benefits.

Only the temporary effects granted by each energy surge - THAC0 bonus and increase in attacks per round - can be dispelled. The divine mark itself, as well as the recurring pulses of energy, cannot be removed by dispel effects.~

@6056 = ~Web
(Conjuration)

Level: 2
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Neg.

A Web spell creates a many-layered mass of strong, sticky strands similar to spider webs but far larger and tougher. The Web spell covers a maximum area of about 15 ft. in radius (roughly the same size as a Fireball). Creatures caught within webs, or simply touching them, become stuck among the gluey fibers. Anyone in the area when the spell is cast must roll a Saving Throw vs. Spell with a -2 penalty. If the Saving Throw is successful, then the creature is free to move out of the area. A failed Saving Throw means the creature is stuck in the webs unable to move. Each round that a creature remains in the web, it must make a Saving Throw or be unable to move.~

@6057 = ~Dragon's Strength~

@6058 = ~Dragon's Strength (Alteration)
Level: 10
Range: Touch
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 6
Are of Effect: One creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell endows the target with the raw power and vitality of a mighty dragon. This surge of strength allows the recipient to perform incredible feats of physical might and endure far greater punishment in combat. However, despite these formidable enhancements, their outward appearance remains unchanged, making the transformation all the more astonishing.

This spell grants the recipient 25 strength, +5 base damage in melee, immunity to Fear and a 25% increase in their base health pool, which can not be dispelled for its duration.~

@6059 = ~Blinding Speed~

@6060 = ~Blinding Speed
This special spell makes the caster so fast, that he can traverse long distances in a blink of an eye, if there are no obstacles in his path. In addition, the number of attacks per round is doubled and this spell can't be dispelled. It lasts for 5 rounds.~

@6061 = ~Chain Sequencer~

@6062 = ~Chain Sequencer
This is a far more dangerous form of standard Sequencer spell. The caster first chooses one spell of levels 1-3 which will be put into the sequencer and stored as an ability just like with any other Sequencer. When used, that selected spell will be cast on all non-invisible hostile creatures in a 15-ft radius from the center chosen by the caster. It is worth mentioning, that spells which require touch will have no effects.~

@6063 = ~Activate Chain Sequencer~

@6064 = ~Non-Detection (Abjuration)
Level: 1
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the wizard makes one creature immune to the first effect that would dispel invisibility from that creature, be it from magical means like True Sight or through Detect Illusions ability.~

@6065 = ~Non-Detection absorbed~

@6066 = ~Target is already under the effects of Improved Invisibility~

@6067 = ~Simulacrum:
This spell creates a duplicate of the caster, which closely resembles the original and acts as a powerful ally. The clone can be controlled freely and can cast spells just like the caster, it will serve the caster for 2 turns. The clone cannot engage in physical combat or use weapons. The spell does not replicate any items the caster is using or wearing. It is created at 60% of the caster's level and can cast spells of up to 3rd level. When the Illusionist reaches level 20, the clone gains access to spells of level 4.~

@6068 = ~Focused Mind Blast~

@6069 = ~Focused Mind Blast:
Expertise with mind-affecting spells and creativity can make for a deadly combination. Enchanters can usurp control over enemy minds by force, or guide and join the minds of those who willingly allow them access. By casting this spell, an enchanter connects with companions from the same party and momentarily focuses on a small area within their vision. Through the enchanter's guidance, a powerful blast of cumulative telepathic energy is sent towards that point, exploding suddenly. Any creature in that area will be severely damaged, regardless of whether it has a mind or not.

The caster can achieve a similar effect alone, but the more party members join forces, the more deadly the attack will be. At level 10, the blast deals 4d6 magical damage plus an additional 2d6 for each party member. This damage increases by 2d6 for the caster and by 1d6 for party members at caster levels 16, 22, 28, 34 and 40, and it bypasses magical resistance. A party member has to be within 50 feet from the center of the spell to contribute in the damage.~

@6070 = ~See Invisible~

@6071 = ~See Invisible
By concentrating intensely, Diviners can pierce through any illusion, allowing them to see things as they truly are for the next 5 rounds. This ability can't be dispelled and it enables the caster to target creatures under the effects of Improved Invisibility and negates any penalties from attacking such creatures with weapons.

Due to the intense focus required, this ability cannot be used in combination with Improved Alacrity and will remove its effects when cast.~

@6072 = ~Glimpse of the Future~

@6073 = ~Glimpse of the Future
This ability targets any single friendly creature without requiring the caster's aura to be cleansed. It sends visions of numerous potential futures to the target, providing insight on how to avoid or mitigate impending danger. The target gains a +20 bonus to all saving throws and armor class for 2 seconds.~

@6074 = ~Abjuration Mastery~

@6075 = ~Abjuration Mastery
With this power a skilled Abjurers can cast any spell of their favored school bypassing the need to cleanse their aura. The chosen spell is uninterruptible and does not need to be prepared in advance. This grants Abjurers an unparalleled edge in battle, allowing them to summon protective and dispelling magic at a moment's notice.

The potency of this ability grows with the caster's experience:

At level 12: Cast spells up to 4th level
At level 14: Cast spells up to 5th level
At level 16: Cast spells up to 6th level
At level 18: Cast spells up to 7th level
At level 20: Cast spells up to 8th level
At level 22 and above: Cast any mage abjuration spell~

@6076 = ~Animal Rage (Enchantment)
Level: 3
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 2 animals
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell Beast Masters targets two animals and turns on their most feral side in a guided way, without the risk of them going berserk or attacking their allies in fury. The animals becomes enraged for 2 turns. While enraged, they gains an additional attack per round, a bonus of +3 to their attack and damage rolls as well as to Armor Class. This spell works only on animals and cannot be dispelled by any means.~

@6077 = ~Hide in Shadows active~

@6078 = ~Hide in Shadows disabled~

@6079 = ~Avoid Death
With extraordinary effort, a high-level rogue can avoid almost certain death. The effect lasts for 1 turn, and during this time, the rogue's Save vs. Death receives a bonus of 5, Hit Points are increased by 20, and the rogue becomes immune to death magic and instant death effects. This ability cannot be dispelled by any means~

@6080 = ~Evasion
A rogue's natural sense of preservation becomes heightened with the use of the Evasion ability. Evasion gives a bonus of 4 to AC and 2 to all Saving Throws. The effect lasts for 6 rounds and cannot be dispelled by any means.~

@6081 = ~Greater Evasion
A more powerful version of Evasion, this ability improves Armor Class by 6 and Saving Throws by 3. In addition, Greater Evasion allows the rogue to move so quickly that <PRO_HISHER> movement rate is increased by 2 (base is 9) and normal missiles have no chance of striking <PRO_HIMHER>. Greater Evasion lasts for 1 turn and cannot be dispelled by any means.

Requires: Evasion~

@6082 = ~Scribe Shield Scroll~

@6083 = ~Scribe Armor Scroll~

@6084 = ~Scribe Blur Scroll~

@6085 = ~Scribe Mirror Image Scroll~

@6086 = ~Scribe Scrolls
This ability allows a rogue to create special versions of low--level spell scrolls that only rogues can use. When the rogue uses this ability, the following scrolls appear in his or her equipment:
1) Luck
2) Mirror Image
3) Blur

Those scrolls allow rogues to cast spells at level 10 to determine their power and duration. The scrolls are unstable and will lose their power and vanish after 4 hours.~

@6087 = ~Animal Fortitude~

@6088 = ~Animal Fortitude (Alteration)
Level: 2
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 2 animals
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell the Beast Master targets two animals, fortifies their natural defenses and amplifies their endurance. For the next two turns the targets will have maximum HP increased by 50% and resistance to physical damage by 15%, additionally the creatures will be immune to spells and effects that would unsummon them. This spell works only on animals.~

@6089 = ~You can cast Animal Summoning I again~

@6090 = ~You can cast Animal Summoning II again~

@6091 = ~You can cast Animal Summoning III again~

@6092 = ~You can cast Animal Summoning IV again~

@6093 = ~By means of this spell, the caster calls 2 Dire Wolves. They will remain under the caster's control for 15 rounds or until slain. The Beast Master can use this ability once per 15 rounds.~

@6094 = ~By means of this spell, the caster calls 2 Brown Bears. They will remain under the caster's control for 15 rounds or until slain. The Beast Master can use this ability once per 15 rounds.~

@6095 = ~By means of this spell, the caster calls 2 Winter Wolves. They will remain under the caster's control for 15 rounds or until slain. The Beast Master can use this ability once per 15 rounds.~

@6096 = ~By means of this spell, the caster calls a powerful Anaconda. The creature will remain under the caster's control for 15 rounds or until slain. The Beast Master can use this ability once per 15 rounds.~

@6097 = ~Hunter's Mark~

@6098 = ~Hunter's Mark:
When using this ability, the Beast Master places a mystical mark on a single enemy. For the next turn, the marked enemy suffers a -2 penalty to their THAC0 against the Beast Master and any animals. The Beast Master and all animals within a 15-foot radius gain a +2 bonus to their damage and THAC0 against the marked enemy. Additionally, all attacks from affected animals against that target will be treated as if made with a +4 weapon for determining if the target can be damaged. All thac0 and damage bonuses/penalties increase by 1 for every 5 levels of the caster.

The Beast Master can use this ability again after 15 rounds or if the target dies.~

@6099 = ~Unified Minds~

@6100 = ~Unified Minds
By invoking this ability, the Beast Master forms a mental bond with one animal companion, linking their senses and instincts into a single, harmonious flow. For 1 turn, as long as the Beast Master and the chosen animal remain within 10 feet of each other, they instinctively protect one another - deflecting blows, alerting each other to danger, and shifting to shield vital areas.

While under this effect, both the Beast Master and the bonded creature receive a -5 bonus to Armor Class and 10% damage resistance against all weapon types. Their shared awareness also shields them from mental interference, granting immunity to fear and protection from confusion, charm, domination, and similar effects, akin to the Chaotic Commands spell.

This ability has no effect if either the Beast Master or the animal is confused, stunned, charmed, feared, or feebleminded at the time of casting or restoring the link. The link is broken if they move more than 10 feet apart, but it will be restored if they come close again before the duration ends.

The effects do not stack with multiple uses.~

@6101 = ~Resist Fire/Resist Cold (Alteration)
Level: 4
Sphere: Protection
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is placed upon a creature by a priest, the creature's body is toughened to withstand heat and cold. The recipient can resist intense heat or cold (whether natural or magical in origin), such as: red-hot charcoal, a large amount of burning oil, flaming swords, fire storms, fireballs, meteor swarms, red dragon's breath, frostbrand swords, ice storms, wands of frost, or white dragon's breath. In all of these cases, the temperature affects the creature to some extent. This spell sets cold and fire resistance of the target to 75%.~

@6102 = ~Negative Plane Protection
(Abjuration)

Level: 4
Sphere: Protection, Necromantic
Range: Touch
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell affords the caster or the touched creature partial protection from undead monsters with Negative Energy Plane connections (such as vampires), and certain weapons and spells that drain energy levels. The Negative Plane Protection spell opens a channel to the Positive Energy Plane, possibly offsetting the effects of the negative energy attack. A protected creature struck by a negative energy attack is protected against any form of level draining for the duration of the spell. The protected creature suffers only normal Hit Point damage from the attack and does not suffer any drain of experience. This spell cannot be cast on the Negative Energy Plane.~

@6103 = ~Disable Trap~

@6104 = ~Trap Disabled~

@6105 = ~Champion's Might~

@6106 = ~Too many instances of Champion's Might, the spell is broken.~

@6107 = ~Protection From Fire (Abjuration)
Level: 3
Sphere: Protection, Elemental (Fire)
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, it sets the target's fire resistance to 75% for its duration which is no longer than five turns or 50 rounds.~

@6108 = ~Protection From Fire (Abjuration)
Level: 3
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, it sets the target's fire resistance to 75% for its duration which is no longer than five turns or 50 rounds.~

@6109 = ~Protection From Cold (Abjuration)
Level: 3
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, it sets the target's cold resistance to 75% for its duration which is no longer than five turns or 50 rounds.~

@6110 = ~Protection From Cold (Abjuration)
Level: 3
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: Creature touched
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, it sets the target's cold resistance to 75% for its duration which is no longer than five turns or 50 rounds.~

@6111 = ~Protection From Lightning 
(Abjuration)

Level: 4
Sphere: Protection, Weather
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 7 
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None 

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's electricity resistance to 75%, partially protecting from electrical attacks such as Lightning Bolt, Shocking Grasp, and so on. The protection will last for the duration of the spell or until successfully dispelled.~

@6112 = ~Protection From Electricity
(Abjuration)

Level: 5
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's electricity resistance to 75%, partially protecting from electrical attacks such as Lightning Bolt, Shocking Grasp, and so on. The protection will last for the duration of the spell or until successfully dispelled.~

@6113 = ~Protection From Acid
(Abjuration)

Level: 5
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature 
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's acid resistance to 75%, partially protecting from acid attacks such as Acid Arrow or a creature's special attacks. This effect lasts for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6114 = ~Protection From Acid
(Abjuration)

Level: 5
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature 
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's acid resistance to 75%, partially protecting from acid attacks such as Acid Arrow or a creature's special attacks. This effect lasts for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6115 = ~Protection From Magic Energy
(Abjuration)

Level: 6
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's magical damage resistance to 75%, partially protecting from all magic-based attacks such as Magic Missile or Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting. This effect lasts for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6116 = ~Protection From The Elements
(Abjuration)

Level: 7
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's elemental resistance to 75%, partially protecting from all elemental attacks - such as fire, cold, acid and electricity, whether magical or non magical - from spells, weapons, wands, breath weapons, etc. The effect of a Protection From The Elements spell lasts 1 round per level of the caster or until dispelled.~

@6117 = ~Protection From Energy
(Abjuration)

Level: 8
Range: Touch
Duration: 5 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When the spell is cast, it sets the target's resistances against all energies to 75%, partially protecting from all energy attacks - such as fire, cold, acid, magic, and electricity, whether from magical or non-magical sources - such as spells, weapons, wands, breath weapons, etc. This excludes any physical attacks and spell-created weapons, such as Enchanted Weapon and Spiritual Hammer. In other words, any physical damage, such as piercing, crushing, or slashing will get through. This effect lasts for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6118 = ~Storm Shield: 
This spell lasts 1 round per level of the caster. It protects the caster from normal missiles and sets his lightning, fire and cold resistances to 75%.~

@6119 = ~Luck
(Enchantment/Charm)

Level: 2
Range: 15 ft.
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

The recipient of this spell gains extraordinary luck for the next 2 turns, receiving a +1 bonus to <PRO_HISHER> Saving Throws, attack rolls, and minimum damage/healing rolls as well as +5% to all thieving skills. Furthermore, damage dice for all effects outside a weapon's base damage is reduced by 1. For example, a 6d6 fireball will do 6d5 damage, and a flaming long sword that deals 1d8+2 slashing plus 1d3 fire damage will deal 1d8+2 slashing plus 1d2 fire damage instead. Multiple casts of Luck do not stack with each other.~

@6120 = ~You can use Hunter's Mark again.~

@6121 = ~Life Link~

@6122 = ~Life Link
(Necromancy)

Level: 6
Sphere: Healing
Range: 30 ft.
Duration: 10 rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: targetted creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the priest links his or her own life force with that of an ally. Each time that ally is dealt damage that would not result in his death, a check is made. If the target's HP is lower than the caster's, then their HP values are immediately swapped. Swapped HP can not exceed the character's max HP value, so it is highly advised to use this spell on a target that has higher max HP than the caster. When more clerics from the same party use this spell, their life threads can become entangled, leading to unforeseen results.

From level 16 each time the target of this spell is hurt, the cleric regenerates 1d4 HP one second later, this value is increased to 1d8 at level 20.~

@6123 = ~Improved Invisibility
(Illusion/Phantasm)

Level: 4
Range: Touch
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell is similar to Invisibility, but the recipient is able to attack by missile discharge, melee combat, or spellcasting while remaining unseen. However, telltale traces - a shimmering - allow an observant opponent to attack the invisible spell recipient. These traces are only noticeable when specifically looked for (after the invisible character has made <PRO_HISHER> presence known). Attacks against the invisible character suffer a -4 penalty to attack rolls.

Note: After making an attack, the wizard is no longer completely invisible. Opponents can target the wizard.~

@6124 = ~Champion's Might
(Alteration)

Level: 6
Sphere: Law
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the priest places a divine mark on the target, which lasts for 15 rounds. A moment later a surge of godly energy flows from the priest's body to the nearest party member with said mark active. This energy greatly enhances combat abilities of the target, granting +1 bonus to THAC0 per 5 levels of the caster (up to +4 at level 20). The target also becomes hasted and his number of attacks per round is increased by one as if Improved Haste was cast on him.

The spell applies its effects every 6 seconds to the nearest marked character for its duration and the effects last for the same amount of time. The target has to be in the caster's range for each pulse of the spell, otherwise he'll have to wait for another pulse to get the benefits.

Only the temporary effects granted by each energy surge - THAC0 bonus, haste, and extra attack - can be dispelled. The divine mark itself, as well as the recurring pulses of energy, cannot be removed by dispel effects.~

@6125 = ~Improved Haste
(Alteration)

Level: 6
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

When casting this spell the caster chooses one target within the spell's range. The affected creature functions at double its normal movement, becomes hasted and gets an additional attack per round. Thus, a creature moving at 6 and attacking once per round would move at 12 and attack thrice per round. Spellcasting and spell effects are not sped up. There are three major differences between the 3rd-level wizard spell Haste and this spell: First, there is no period of fatigue following the expiration of the spell; second, this spell will only affect a single creature; third, this spell increase the number attacks per round of the hasted creature by additional 1 point. This spell also negates the effects of a Slow spell, but it is not cumulative with itself or with other similar magic. Its effects will last for the duration or until dispelled~

@6126 = ~Flurry of Blows:
Agility and prowess are key factors that allow a master of hand-to-hand combat survive in a fight against heavily armed bandits and spell-wielding sorcerers. Trained monks are capable of engaging their opponent with extraordinary speed, making them hasted and increasing their number of attacks per round by 1. This ability lasts for 3 rounds + 1 round / level and can not be dispelled by any external sources.~

@6127 = ~Trap Ward~

@6128 = ~Trap Ward
(Divination)

Level: 2
Sphere: Divination
Range: 0
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None 

When a priest casts a Trap Ward spell, he or she can choose one of two subspells:
- Deactivate Traps - this spell targets the caster and allows it to deactivate any removable trap without getting harmed. For the next 6 seconds the caster can safely enter a trapped region or open a trapped chest and the spell will disable the trap instead of triggering it.
- Find Traps - this spell reveals all traps in the caster's vicinity every 6 seconds for the next 3 turns.

A trap is any device or magical ward that meets three criteria: it can inflict a sudden or unexpected result; the spellcaster would view the result as undesirable or harmful; and the creator specifically intended the harmful or undesirable result as such. Thus traps include glyphs and similar spells or devices.~

@6129 = ~Trap Ward
(Divination)

Level: 3
Sphere: Divination
Range: 0
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None 

When a Mage casts a Trap Ward spell, he or she can choose one of two subspells:
- Deactivate Traps - this spell targets the caster and allows it to deactivate any one-time trap without getting harmed. For the next 6 seconds the caster can safely enter a trapped region or open a trapped chest and the spell will disable the trap instead of triggering it.
- Find Traps - this spell reveals all traps in the caster's vicinity every 6 seconds for the next 3 turns.

A trap is any device or magical ward that meets three criteria: it can inflict a sudden or unexpected result; the spellcaster would view the result as undesirable or harmful; and the creator specifically intended the harmful or undesirable result as such. Thus traps include glyphs and similar spells or devices.~


@6130 = ~Remove Area Trap~

@6131 = ~Deactivate Traps~

@6132 = ~Protection from traps ended.~

@6133 = ~This spell heals the character by 8 + 5% of his max Hit Points.~

@6134 = ~This spell heals the character by 14 + 15% of his max  Hit Points.~

@6135 = ~This spell heals the character by 17 + 20% of his max  Hit Points.~

@6136 = ~This spell heals the character by 27 + 25% of his max  Hit Points.~

@6137 = ~Shield Mind and Body~

@6138 = ~Shield Mind~

@6139 = ~Shield Body~

@6140 = ~Shield Mind and Body
(Abjuration)

Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Upon casting, the spell envelops the caster in two distinct layers of shielding energy.
The Shield Body layer fortifies the caster's physical form, granting immunity to poisons, blindness, and deafness, while also clearing the air that the caster inhales, protecting from poisonous and acidic cloud effects.
The Shield Mind layer grants mental clarity and protects from all forms of fear, sleep, berserk, mind control and any similar effects.~

@6141 = ~Ray of Fragmentation (Evocation)
Level: 4
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Once cast on a golem, this powerful spell will penetrate the creature's magic resistance and will inflict inerrable damage. The spell will also affect up to 2 other golems standing nearby. The amount of damage depends on the golem type according the following table:

- Flesh, Stone, Clay, Sand and Iron golems: 4D8
- Asylum Scouts, Coin, Gem, Amber, Brain and Adamantite golems: 2D8
- Ice and Elemental golems: 1D8

Other types of golems cannot be affected by the spell and will take no damage.~

@6142 = ~Poison
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Range: 15 ft.
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Special

Through this spell, the caster can inject strong poison into the body of his target. The damage inflicted depends on the level of the caster as detailed below:
 7–9th level: 2d8 + 2/round
 10–12th level: 3d8 + 3/round
 13–14th level: 4d8 + 4/round
 15–16th level: 6d8 + 5/round
 17+ level: 8d8 + 6/round
Those who make their Saving Throws against Poison only suffer the initial portion of the damage.~

@6143 = ~Earthquake
(Alteration)

Level: 7
Sphere: Elemental (Earth)
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: Special


When casting this spell, the caster selects 3 points in his range of vision as the epicenters of small yet powerful tremors, each with an 12-foot diameter. All creatures in the area suffer 2d6 crushing damage that bypasses Magic Resistance and drop to the ground for 1 round. A successful Saving Throw vs. Spell negates the fall.

As the caster gains experience, the spell becomes more potent: at level 17, the number of tremor areas increases to 4, and at level 20, it rises to 5.

This spell will affect both enemies and friends of the caster's, so care must be taken in its use. Tremor areas can overlap to increase the damage output to a smaller group of creatures.~

@6144 = ~Blessing of Talos~

@6145 = ~Hand of Undoing (Necromancy)
Level: 7
Range: Touch
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: One golem
Saving Throw: None

This powerful spell enables the caster to focus his life energy towards a golem and apply a massive shock to the target's internal animating force upon touching it. The spell will inflict considerable damage, which depends on the golem type according the following table:

- Flesh, Stone, Clay, Sand and Iron golems: 8D8 +40
- Ice, Elemental, Coin, Gem, Amber, Brain and Adamantite golems: 4D8 +20
- Greater Elemental, Ultra, Supreme and any other unique powerful golems: 2D8 +10.

Additionally when the mage starts casting this spell, he or she becomes completely invisible to any golem for 4 seconds, which makes this spell easier to cast without interruption.~

@6146 = ~Call Woodland Beings
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 4
Sphere: Animal, Summoning 
Range: 25 ft.
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 7 
Area of Effect: Special 
Saving Throw: None 

This spell summons forth a nymph to assist the party. The nymph has several priest spells at her disposal and will use them in the best interests of the party (these include Barkskin, Hold Person and a few healing spells). She will remain under the caster's control until slain or the spell's duration expires.~

@6147 = ~Whirlwind~

@6148 = ~Whirlwind
(Conjuration)

Level: Quest
Range: 5 ft.
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: Special

This spell creates a small whirlwind near the caster. The caster has no control over the whirlwind and it will fly around randomly, harming friend and foe alike. The caster is immune to his/her own spell, and elementals and other huge creatures are also unaffected. If a creature is caught in the path of the whirlwind, it takes 4d8+4 electrical damage that grants no saving throw, 4d8+4 slashing damage which allows a saving throw, and must make a successful save vs breath or be stunned for 2 rounds. The whirlwind can't hit the same creature more often than once per 3 seconds. All effects of this spell bypass magic resistance.~

@6149 = ~Ice Spikes~

@6150 = ~Ice Spikes
(Evocation)

Level: Quest
Range: 0
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 18-ft. cone with 90-deg. arc
Saving Throw: 1/2

When this spell is cast, sharp, jagged ice spikes erupt from the ground in a cone-shaped area originating from the caster's hand and extending outward 18 feet in a 90-degree arc. The ice spikes pierce through enemies within the area, dealing 10d6+10 points of piercing and cold damage. Creatures who successfully save vs breath with a -2 penalty take half damage. The caster can control the area where the spikes grow ensuring that only enemies are affected. This spell ignores enemy magic resistance.~

@6151 = ~Fissure~

@6152 = ~Fissure
(Evocation)

Level: Quest
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 10-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the ground beneath each enemy in a 10-foot radius of a point chosen by the caster splits open, creating small fissures that spew magma and acidic gases. Each affected enemy suffers 10d6 fire damage and 4d6 acid damage that ignores magic resistance. The spell also reduces fire resistance of all creatures that have fire resistance lower than 100% by 5% for 2 rounds.

The fissures are precise and magically controlled, targeting only enemies while leaving allies unharmed.~

@6153 = ~Acid Wave~

@6154 = ~Acid Wave
(Conjuration)

Level: Quest
Range: 40 feet
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 5-foot wide wave
Saving Throw: Special

This spell summons a wave of acidic substances that moves in the direction willed by the caster, striking all in its path with massive force. The wave deals 12d6 crushing  and acid damage, in addition, there is a 25% chance a creature struck is stunned for one round. If the creature struck makes a successful save vs breath with a -4 penalty, the damage is reduced by half and the creature avoids being stunned. This spell ignores enemy magic resistance.~

@6155 = ~Acid Circle~

@6156 = ~Animal Summoning IV~

@6157 = ~Lloth's Blessing~

@6158 = ~Mind Flayer Focused Mind Blast~

@6159 = ~Soften Mind~

@6160 = ~Mind Flayer Shared Mind Blast~

@6161 = ~Emotion: Hope~

@6162 = ~Emotion: Hope
(Enchantment/Charm)

Level: 4
Range: 50 ft.
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

This spell instills a sense of hope within the area of effect, granting all affected friendly creatures a morale boost along with a +2 bonus to their Saving Throws, attack rolls, and damage rolls. While it negates the effects of Emotion: Hopelessness, it does not provide immunity to the spell and can be overridden by a subsequent casting of Emotion: Hopelessness.~

@6163 = ~Minor Sequencer
(Generalist)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

This spell allows a wizard to store two spells and activate them both at the same time from <PRO_HISHER> Special Ability button. Both spells must be of 2nd level or lower. To create a sequencer, a Mage must memorize not only Minor Sequencer but also the spells <PRO_HESHE> intends to store in it (a Sorcerer can store spells of any level for which <PRO_HESHE> still has spell slots). After casting Minor Sequencer, the player will be prompted to choose the sequenced spells from those <PRO_HESHE> has memorized.

A sequencer lasts until activated and, once used, releases its spells immediately (no casting time). The Special Ability icon also disappears until the next time a sequencer is formed. A wizard can possess only one Minor Sequencer at a time, and it may not be given to other characters.~

@6164 = ~Spell Sequencer
(Generalist)

Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

This spell allows a wizard to store three spells and activate them all at the same time from <PRO_HISHER> Special Ability button. All spells must be of 4th level or lower. To create a sequencer, a Mage must memorize not only Spell Sequencer but also the spells <PRO_HESHE> intends to store in it (a Sorcerer can store spells of any level for which <PRO_HESHE> still has spell slots). After casting Spell Sequencer, the player will be prompted to choose the sequenced spells from those <PRO_HESHE> has memorized.

A sequencer lasts until activated and, once used, releases its spells immediately (no casting time). The Special Ability icon also disappears until the next time a sequencer is formed. A wizard can possess only one Spell Sequencer at a time, and it may not be given to other characters.~

@6165 = ~Contingency (Generalist)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 1 day/level
Casting Time: 0
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Upon casting this spell the wizard is allowed to choose a spell out of his repertoire of known spells. One spell level for every three levels of the caster is allowed up to 18th level or 6th level spells. Once the spell is chosen the caster is allowed to choose a condition of some kind from the list provided. The starting condition can be anything from reaching 10% of his/her hit points to an enemy being sighted. Once this starting condition is satisfied the spell that was chosen will be cast automatically. For example a 12th level wizard could place the spell stoneskin in a contingency with the starting condition being 'the wizard reaches 50% of his hit points'. Then in combat once the wizard is reduced to 50% of his hit points or below, stoneskin would be immediately cast upon him. This requires no action by the wizard, it happens automatically and instantaneously. The limitation of this spell is that the target of the spell placed in the contingency must be the caster. Therefor it cannot be an offensive spell and cannot target any other party members.~

@6166 = ~Chain Contingency (Generalist)
Level: 9
Range: 0
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 0
Area of Effect: The Caster
Saving Throw: None

Chain contingency channels some of the magical energy of the mage and releases it only under certain circumstances. Basically, the mage chooses three spells, which will be released under certain conditions such as being hit by an enemy. When this condition occurs all three spells are cast immediately. Spells of 8th level or lower may be used in the contingency.~

@6167 = ~Spell Trigger
(Generalist) 

Level: 8
Range: 0 
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: The caster 
Saving Throw: None 

This spell allows a wizard to store spells in a magical ability (accessed via the Special Ability button) that is created by the spell. This item, the trigger, can store three spells to be released simultaneously, all of which must be of 6th level or lower. A wizard can only possess one spell trigger at a time, and the trigger may not be given to other characters. Once the spell trigger is used, the icon will disappear from the Special Ability button.~

@6168 = ~Aegis of Faith~

@6169 = ~Aegis of Faith
Through prayer and devotion, the cleric grants themselves a protective blessing that safeguards their magical defenses. For the next turn, any effects that targets and removes specific protections will be nullified. This spell does not protect against spells and effects that dispel all types of effects at once, like Remove Magic or Purge Magic.

This blessing cannot be dispelled and remains active for its full duration.~

@6170 = ~Chant
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 2
Sphere: Combat 
Range: 0 
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 4 
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius 
Saving Throw: None 

By means of the Chant spell, the priest brings special favor upon <PRO_HISHER>self and <PRO_HISHER> party and causes harm to <PRO_HISHER> enemies. When the Chant spell is completed, all the priest's allies within the area of effect gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls, minimum damage, and Saving Throws. Furthermore, damage dice for all effects outside a weapon's base damage is reduced by 1. The priest's enemies suffer the opposite effects.

Multiple chants are not cumulative.~

@6171 = ~Critical Strike
A master warrior knows exactly when and where to strike for maximum impact. Once per day, <PRO_HESHE> can focus <PRO_HISHER> attacks with unparalleled precision. For the next 4 rounds, <PRO_HESHE> gains a +45% chance to land a critical hit. This effect lasts until the duration ends or after 12 successful attacks, whichever comes first.

Requires: Power Attack~

@6172 = ~Whirlwind Attack
This ability allows the warrior to unleash a flurry of super-fast blows. The ability increases the number of attacks per round by 1 and then doubles the final value, but one's THAC0 and damage suffer a 4 point penalty. The Whirlwind Attack lasts for 3 rounds. This ability disregards bonuses to attacks per round from Improved Haste and similar spells/abilities, which were used prior to Whirlwind Attack, but does not remove them.

This ability can be picked only once~

@6173 = ~Greater Whirlwind Attack
A more powerful version of the Whirlwind Attack, Greater Whirlwind gives the warrior the same bonuses without penalties. This ability can be picked only once.

Requires: Whirlwind Attack~

@6174 = ~War Cry
Letting loose a battle cry that fuels both rage and resolve, the warrior enters a heightened state of combat. For 1 turn, <PRO_HESHE> gains double the normal number of attacks per round, and cannot be affected by Haste or Slow effects during this time. This reckless exertion comes at a price - every 2 rounds, <PRO_HISHER> fatigue level increases by 1. This ability disregards bonuses to attacks per round from Improved Haste and similar spells/abilities, which were used prior to War Cry, but does not remove them.~

@6175 = ~War Cry~

@6176 = ~Improved Hasted~

@6177 = ~Flurry of Blows
Agility and prowess are key factors that allow a master of hand-to-hand combat survive in a fight against heavily armed bandits and spell-wielding sorcerers. Trained monks are capable of engaging their opponent with extraordinary speed, making them hasted and doubling their number of attacks per round. This ability lasts for 1 turn and can not be dispelled by any external sources.~

@6178 = ~Perform Ritual
Level: Quest
Range: 0
Duration: 1 Turn
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: The Caster
Saving Throw: None

PERFORM RITUAL: This ability allows the Avenger to perform a secret ritual that was perfected by members of the order. It is the ultimate reason why the druid has to sacrifice his connection to the nature. When the ritual is initiated, the Avenger attains a state of etherealness, as if stepping outside the material plane. Entering such state allows the Avenger to move faster and avoid constrictive areas. Due to his partial presense in the physical world, the druid becomes harder to hit by the ordinary melee attacks. Any type of magic that affects the druid's movement has no effect on <PRO_HIMHER>. The duration of the ability equals one turn.

Abilities:
 - +5 Bonus to Armor Class
 - +1 Bonus to movement speed
 - Doubled number of attacks per round, disregarding bonuses from Improved Haste
 - Immunity to Web, Improved Web and Vortex Web
 - Immunity to Slow, Hold and Stun effects~

@6179 = ~Acrobatic Combat
By using this ability, a high level swashbuckler can improve his agility and fighting expertise (in both defense and attack) to an extraordinary level. Acrobatic Combat grants +4 bonus to AC against all weapon types (not the base AC), +1/2 attacks per round and +4 bonus to THAC0 for 5 rounds.~

@6180 = ~Ghost's Grace~

@6181 = ~Ghost's Grace
Through extensive training and unmatched agility, the Assassin can evade physical attacks with incredible precision. This High-Level Ability grants the Assassin immunity to the physical damage of two incoming attacks per round, using their swift reflexes to dodge the blows. However, while the physical portion of the attack is negated, any additional effects or enchantments on the strike still apply. This ability lasts for 1 turn.~

@6182 = ~Analyze Opponent~

@6183 = ~Analyze Opponent
The Assassin employs their extraordinary observational skills to identify and exploit the weaknesses of enemies within a certain range. Through careful analysis of their movements and vulnerabilities, the Assassin can perform backstabs on creatures that would normally be too alert and immune to such attacks for the next 5 rounds.~

@6184 = ~Extend Lifespan

A high-level rogue's astute powers of observation allow them to improve their health by incorporation of their companions' training regiments. Effect: Adds +10 Max HP permanently. Can be picked up to 3 times.~

@6185 = ~Assassination
Drawing on every trick learned through countless battles, the Thief can turn the next ten successful attacks within five rounds into backstabs.
Assassins, with their deadly precision, gain an improved version of this ability, allowing for fifteen such attacks.~

@6186 = ~Lesser Hardiness~

@6187 = ~Summon Swanmay~

@6188 = ~Increase Spell Duration II~

@6189 = ~Increase Spell Duration II

High-level priests devout to their god can receive a special blessing from their worshipped deity, which causes the magic of their spells to dissipate more slowly than normal. This blessing extends the base duration of clerical spells by 50%.

This ability does not extend the duration of the following:
-Spells that apply their effects periodically (like True Seeing or Continual Cure)
-Spells that apply different effects to allies and enemies (like Chant)
-Improved versions of spells cast by Cleric kits (like Armor of Faith for all Clerics or Righteous Magic for Priest of Tyr)
-Spell-like abilities that are not memorized in Priest spellbook (like Summon Archdeva)~

@6190 = ~Straight Through the Heart~

@6191 = ~Straight Through the Heart
With flawless precision and a ruthless instinct for weakness, the Thief delivers devastating strikes where it hurts the most. For the next three successful melee attacks the backstab multiplier is increased by 1. Maximum duration of this ability is 1 round.

This ability can be used instantly at any moment, without wasting character's action.~

@6192 = ~Marked for the Kill~

@6193 = ~Marked for the Kill
With a keen hunter's eye, the Stalker identifies and exploits the subtle flaws in an enemy's defenses. The target loses any immunity to backstab until any damage is dealt to him or until one round passes.

This ability does not take up the creature's action and can be used an indefinite number of times, however no more often than once per 5 rounds. This time is decreased to 4 rounds at level 10, 3 rounds at level 20 and finally to 2 rounds at level 30.~

@6194 = ~Can't use Marked for the Kill~

@6195 = ~Armor (Conjuration)
Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: None

By means of this spell, the wizard creates a magical field of force that serves as if it were scale mail armor. It sets the wizard's base armor class to 6, and grants an additional +3 bonus to AC against piercing and slashing weapons. It is cumulative with Dexterity and, in the case of fighter/mages, with the shield bonus. Due to the armor's magical nature it also increases elemental resistances by 10%. The armor spell does not hinder movement, adds no weight or encumbrance, nor does it prevent spellcasting. It lasts until successfully dispelled or until the duration runs out.~

@6196 = ~Shield (Evocation)
Level: 1
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, an invisible barrier comes into being in front of the wizard. It sets the wizard's base armor class to 6, and grants an additional +3 bonus to AC against missile and blunt weapons. It is cumulative with Dexterity and, in the case of fighter/mages, with the shield bonus. Due to the shield's magical nature it also increases resistance to magical damage by 15%. The shield spell does not hinder movement, adds no weight or encumbrance, nor does it prevent spellcasting. The effect lasts for the duration of the spell or until dispelled.~

@6197 = ~Silence 15' Radius (Alteration)
Level: 2
Sphere: Guardian
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 rounds
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 15-foot-radius sphere
Saving Throw: Neg

Upon casting this spell, complete silence prevails in the affected area. All sound is stopped: conversation is impossible and spells cannot be cast. Each creature in the area must make a saving throw vs. spells at -2; if the save is failed, then they are silenced for the duration of the spell. Note that this spell does not continue to affect the area after being cast; only those in the area at the time of the casting are affected by the silence.~

@6198 = ~Fireshield (Blue)
(Evocation)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

The blue Fireshield protects the user from cold damage by surrounding the caster with a shield of ice flame. This shield not only grants the user 50% Cold Resistance, but also protects the caster from attacks made within a 5-ft. radius around the caster. An opponent that hits the caster with any weapons or spells within this radius suffers 1d8+2 cold damage.

Additionally, while the Fireshield is active, there is a 20% chance every 3 seconds to automatically remove Web effects and any Insect-based spells affecting the caster, like Insect Plague or Creeping Doom. The intense cold of the shield causes sticky webs to become brittle and shatter, while freezing temperatures drive off or kill swarming insects.~

@6199 = ~Fireshield (Red)
(Evocation)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

The red Fireshield protects the user from fire damage by surrounding the caster with a shield of flame. This shield does not only grant the user a 50% Fire Resistance, but also protects <PRO_HIMHER> from attacks made from within a 5-ft. radius around <PRO_HIMHER>. An opponent that hits the caster with any weapons or spells within this radius suffers 1d8+2 points of fire damage.

Additionally, while the Fireshield is active, there is a 20% chance every 3 seconds to automatically remove Web effects and any Insect-based spells affecting the caster, such as Insect Plague or Creeping Doom. The searing heat of the flame incinerates sticky webs and burns away swarms of biting insects.~

@6200 = ~Acid Shield
(Evocation, Alteration)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

The Acid Shield protects the user from acid damage by surrounding the caster with a shield of corrosive substance. This shield does not only grant the user a 50% Acid Resistance, but also protects <PRO_HIMHER> from attacks made from within a 5-ft. radius around <PRO_HIMHER>. An opponent that hits the caster with any weapons or spells within this radius suffers 1d8+2 points of acid damage.

Additionally, while the Acid Shield is active, there is a 20% chance every 3 seconds to automatically remove Web effects and any Insect-based spells affecting the caster, such as Insect Plague or Creeping Doom. The corrosive fumes dissolve webs and prove lethal to lesser insects.~

@6201 = ~Aura of Flaming Death
(Evocation, Alteration)

Level: Quest
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round/2 levels
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

This spell causes the caster to be enveloped by an aura of intense flame that both injures opponents and protects the caster from damage. This shield not only increases the user's Fire Resistance by 90% and an AC bonus of 4, but also protects <PRO_HIMHER> from attacks made within a 5-ft. radius. An opponent that hits the caster with any weapons or spells within this radius suffers 2d10+2 fire damage. In addition, the intense heat protects the caster from all non-magical weapons, melee or missile.

Additionally, there is a 40% chance every 3 seconds to automatically remove Web effects and any Insect-based spells affecting the caster, such as Insect Plague or Creeping Doom. The overwhelming magical flames burn through nearly anything that would otherwise cling or swarm.

These effects will remain for the spell's duration and won't be dispellable.~

@6202 = ~The icy flames make the webs brittle and they shatter.~

@6203 = ~The freezing aura kills the swarming insects.~

@6204 = ~The flames burn away the clinging webs.~

@6205 = ~The searing heat incinerates the swarming insects.~

@6206 = ~Corrosive fumes dissolve the sticky webs.~

@6207 = ~The acid melts the swarming insects.~

@6208 = ~You can't cast Life Link on yourself.~

@6209 = ~Spellstrike (Abjuration)
Level: 9
Range: Visual sight of caster
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Target Creature
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast at a target creature, it will dispel all of the magical protections that surround that creature. This includes: Minor Globe Of Invulnerability, Spell Immunity (except SI: Abjuration), Globe Of Invulnerability, Spell Turning and Spell Shield. The target's magic resistance, if any, does not affect this spell.~

@6210 = ~Charge~

@6211 = ~Unholy Blight
(Necromancy)

Level: 3
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Special

This spell calls upon energy from the Negative Energy Plane in order to open a channel between it and the targets. The result is that any good or neutral creatures within the spell's area of effect take 1d4 points of damage per level of the caster, or half damage upon a successful Saving Throw vs. Spell. If the victims fail their Saving Throw, they also receive a -2 penalty to all their rolls for 4 rounds.~

@6212 = ~Nature's Beauty
Illusion/Phantasm
Sphere: Elemental
Level: 7
Range: Caster
Duration: 3 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast, the caster becomes a radiant embodiment of nature's perfection, a vision so breathtaking that it halts all actions from those who behold it. For 3 rounds, the caster cannot be targeted or attacked by most humanoid creatures, no matter if friend or foe, as their senses are overwhelmed with awe and reverence.

Affected creature types include:
Humans, Elves, Dwarves, Halflings, Gnomes, Half-elves, Half-orcs, Goblinoids, Lycanthropes, Orcs, Ogres, Trolls, Gnolls, Kobolds, Lizardfolk, Sahuagin, Yuan-ti, and Giant-kin.

Creatures with alien minds or strong psychic resistance, such as Githyanki, Kuo-Toa, and extraplanar entities, are unaffected. They can interact with the caster normally.

The caster may act freely during this time, but is still vulnerable to area effects, traps, or magical effects already in place.

This spell may only be cast once per turn, but is undispellable.~

@6213 = ~Nature's Beauty~

@6214 = ~Can't use Nature's Beauty~

@6215 = ~Stoneskin
(Alteration)

Level: 4
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: Single creature
Saving Throw: None 

When a wizard casts this powerful spell upon a target, an outer skin of stone will move up from the ground, completely covering the target. This skin is of course magical and will hinder the target in no way. The effect of this is to protect the target from physical attacks such as melee weapons and projectiles. For every 2 levels of the caster, an additional skin is gained upon casting. For example, a 10th-level wizard would create 5 skins while a 20th-level wizard would create 10. For each skin the target possesses, the spell will stop one attack, so a 10th-level wizard would be protected from the first 5 attacks, but the 6th would affect the target normally. The skins will remain on the target until he or she is affected by a Dispel Magic, all of the skins are removed due to physical attacks, or the spell duration expires. It is important to note that this will not protect the target from any magical attacks, such as Fireball.~

@6216 = ~Mend Light Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 1
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the shaman causes 8 points + 3% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body to be healed. This healing cannot affect creatures without corporeal bodies, nor can it cure wounds of creatures not living or of extraplanar origin.~

@6217 = ~Mend Medium Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 3
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the shaman heals 14 points + 9% of wound or other injury damage from the creature's body. This healing cannot affect creatures without corporeal bodies, nor can it cure wounds of creatures not living or of extraplanar origin.~

@6218 = ~Mend Serious Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell is a more potent version of the Mend Light Wounds spell. The shaman calls upon the spirits and mends 17 points + 12% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body. This healing cannot affect noncorporeal, nonliving, or extraplanar creatures.~

@6219 = ~Mend Critical Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 5
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

The Mend Critical Wounds spell is a very potent version of the Mend Light Wounds spell. The shaman calls upon the spirits and mends 27 points + 15% of damage from wounds or other injuries. The spell does not affect creatures without corporeal bodies, those of extraplanar origin, or those not living.~

@6220 = ~Mend Group
(Necromancy)

Level: 5
Sphere: Healing
Range: 15-ft.
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: None

When casting this spell, the shaman reaches out to the spirits of his companions and wills them to mend the harm done to their physical bodies. Upon completion, all party members within a 15-ft. radius of the shaman are healed 15 Hit Points. Curing is permanent only insofar as the creature does not sustain further damage; caused wounds will heal - or can be cured - just as any normal injury.~

@6221 = ~Healing Ward
(Necromancy)

Level: 7
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 10 rounds
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

With this powerful spell the shaman places a protective ward that imbues one creature with the ability to regenerate. This regeneration will mend any wounds and even regenerate lost limbs. The creature affected will regain 2 Hit Points per second. The effect lasts for 10 rounds or until dispelled. This effect is cumulative with itself and with other sources of regeneration.~

@6222 = ~Cure Light Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 1
Sphere: Healing
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell and laying <PRO_HISHER> hand upon a creature, the priest causes 8 points + 5% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body to be healed. This healing cannot affect creatures without corporeal bodies, nor can it cure wounds of creatures not living or of extraplanar origin.

Curing is permanent only insofar as the creature does not sustain further damage; caused wounds will heal - or can be cured - just as any normal injury.~


@6223 = ~Cure Serious Wounds
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Sphere: Healing 
Range: Touch 
Duration: Permanent 
Casting Time: 7 
Area of Effect: 1 creature 
Saving Throw: None 

This spell is a more potent version of the Cure Light Wounds spell. The priest lays <PRO_HISHER> hand upon a creature and heals 17 points +20% of wound or other injury damage to the creature's body. This healing cannot affect noncorporeal, nonliving, or extraplanar creatures.~

@6224 = ~Summon Nishruu
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 6
Range: 120 ft.
Duration: 1 round/level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

By casting the Summon Nishruu spell, a wizard calls into existence a magical being of considerable power: the nishruu. At first glance, this appears to be some sort of mist, but upon closer examination, this boiling, churning red mass of vapors and shapes moves with a life of its own. Drawn toward magic like a moth to the flame, the nishruu feed on the energies surrounding and used by wizards. Luckily, there is no question as to the loyalty of the creature, and it will not attack its summoner even though it would like nothing better. The nishruu have no physical attacks at all, although physical attacks can hurt them. Each time a nishruu touches a target wizard and wraps its tendrils around him, the wizard loses 1 spell slot of levels 1-4 for 2 turns. The nishruu is completely immune to magic (except for Death Spell), and magic will actually heal it. The creature will remain under the wizard's control until slain or until the spell's duration expires.~

@6225 = ~Summon Hakeashar
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 7
Range: 120 ft.
Duration: 8 rounds + 1 round/level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

This spell is similar to the 6th-level wizard spell Summon Nishruu. The hakeashar, in fact, is a more powerful version of the nishruu, with more Hit Points, better attacks, and immunity to normal weapons.

By casting the Summon Hakeashar spell, the wizard calls into existence a magical being of considerable power: the hakeashar. At first glance, this appears to be some sort of mist, but upon closer examination, this boiling, churning gray mass of vapors and shapes moves with a life of its own. Drawn toward magic like a moth to the flame, the hakeashar feeds on the energies surrounding and used by wizards. Luckily, there is no question as to the loyalty of the creature and it will not attack its summoner even though it would like nothing better. The hakeashar has no physical attacks at all, although physical attacks can hurt them. Each time a hakeashar touches a target wizard and wraps its tendrils around him, two things happen: First, all magical items with charges in the possession of the target will be drained by 1 charge, destroying them if only 1 charge was left; second, it causes the wizard to lose 1 spell slot of levels 1-5 for 2 turns. The hakeashar is completely immune to magic, and magic will actually heal it. The creature will remain under the wizard's control until slain or the spell's duration expires.~

@6226 = ~Continual Cure
(Necromancy)

Level: 7
Sphere: Healing
Range: 0
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting time: 5
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Continual Cure cures the cleric for 27 points of damage, and continues to do so every round of the spell's duration. The spell also cures effects of poison and disease, and removes fear each round as well. These effects will remain for the spell's duration and can't be dispelled.~

@6227 = ~Can't use Purify Aura~

@6228 = ~Immunity: Divination
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Casting this powerful spell makes Priestess of Shar immune to all divination spells for the duration of the spell. All spells of this school will not be able to harm or aid the caster for the duration of this spell (except those spells which can only affect their casters). This includes all spells from this school, including any priest spells that might benefit the caster.~

@6229 = ~Lay On Hands

The character channels positive energy to heal the touched creature of 5 Hit Points per level of the caster up till 170.~

@6230 = ~Power Word, Silence
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 6
Range: 90 ft.
Duration: 3 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

In using this spell, the wizard points at an individual and utters the Power Word. The creature targeted must have less than 90 Hit Points and gets no Saving Throw. For the next 3 rounds, that creature cannot make any sound. This silence completely foils any spells that require verbal components. The only ways to counter this spell are either a Dispel Magic or a Vocalize spell.~

@6231 = ~Flame Strike
(Evocation)

Level: 5
Sphere: Combat
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: 1/2 

When the priest calls down a Flame Strike spell, a vertical column of fire roars downward in the exact location called for by the caster. The target must roll a Saving Throw vs. Breath with a -2 penalty. Failure means the creature sustains 1d8 points of damage per level of the caster; otherwise, the damage is halved.~

@6232 = ~Chaos
(Enchantment/Charm)

Level: 6
Sphere: Chaos
Range: 35 ft.
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round/6 levels
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Special

This spell causes confusion in one or more enemy creatures within the area, creating indecision and the inability to take effective action. All enemy creatures within the area of effect are allowed Saving Throws vs. Spell with a -4 penalty. Those successfully saving are unaffected by the spell. Those who fail their Saving Throws will either go berserk, stand confused, or wander about. The spell lasts for 5 rounds + 1 round per 6 levels of the caster (up to 8 rounds at level 18), or until a successful Dispel Magic is cast.~

@6233 = ~Prismatic Spray
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: 15-ft.-long cone 
Saving Throw: Special

When casting this spell, the wizard causes seven shimmering multicolored rays of light to flash from <PRO_HISHER> hand, portraying all colors of the visible spectrum. Any creature with fewer than 8 Hit Dice struck by a ray is blinded for 5 rounds, regardless of any other effect. All creatures caught within the area of effect will be touched by 1 or 2 of the rays, each of which has a different power and purpose:

  Red — Inflicts 20 points of damage with no save.
  Orange — Inflicts 40 points of damage; Save vs. Breath for half.
  Yellow — Inflicts 80 points of damage; Save vs. Spell for half.
  Green — Save vs. Poison or die; survivors take 20 points of poison damage.
  Blue — Inflicts 70 points of damage; Save vs. Spell for half.
  Indigo — Inflicts 50 points of damage; Save vs. Breath for half.
  Violet — Inflicts 30 points of damage with no save.
  
This spell affects only enemies.~

@6234 = ~Globe of Blades
(Evocation)
Level: Quest
Sphere: Guardian/ Creation
Range: 0
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: Special

The priest employs this spell to set up a globe of razor-sharp blades. These whirl and flash around the caster, creating a dangerous barrier. The barrier deals 4D4 points of slashing damage twice per round to any hostile creature in 5ft radius from the caster. The blades are considered as a +5 weapon to determine what creatures can be hit. Creatures under the effect of Globe of Blades, Blade Barrier, Stoneskin or Ironskins are immune to the damage caused by this spell.

This spell will last for 1 turn and cannot be removed or dispelled.~

@6235 = ~Divine spells cast at lower level~

@6236 = ~Seeking Sword disappears when you touch it.~

@6237 = ~Add Long Sword Proficiency~

@6238 = ~After many hours of training with Seeking Sword, the priest can gain even more prowess with the weapon. This passive skill gives additional Long Sword Proficiency~

@6239 = ~Grease
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 1
Range: 30 ft.
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Neg.

A Grease spell covers a material surface with a slippery layer of a fatty, greasy nature for one turn. Any creature entering the area or caught in it when the spell is cast must save vs. Spell at +2 or the substance will cover them impeding their movements. Those who fail their save can move, albeit very slowly, for the rest of the round. Those who remain in the area are allowed a Saving Throw each round until they escape the area.~

@6240 = ~Chain Lightning 
(Invocation/Evocation)

Level: 6
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Special 
Saving Throw: 1/2 

When the wizard casts Chain Lightning, arcs of electrical energy burst from <PRO_HISHER> fingertips. These brilliant arcs of lightning leap at all enemies near the caster, burning them with electrical damage. The lightning causes 2d6 + 1d6 points of damage for every 2 levels of the caster up to 12d6 at level 20. If the target of the lightning saves vs. Spell, only half damage is inflicted. Thus, a 12th-level wizard will cause 8d6 damage to a victim (4d6 if the victim makes <PRO_HISHER> Saving Throw vs. Breath).~

@6241 = ~Larloch's Minor Drain 
(Necromancy)

Level: 1
Range: 30 ft.
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

With this spell, the wizard drains the life force from a target and adds it to <PRO_HISHER> own. The target creature suffers 4 damage, while the Mage gains the same amount. If the Mage goes over <PRO_HISHER> maximum Hit Point total with this spell, <PRO_HESHE> loses any extra Hit Points after 1 turn.

This spell bypasses Magic Resistance.~

@6242 = ~Dragon's Breath
(Any School)

Level: 10
Range: 320 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius
Saving Throw: Special

This spell causes a disembodied head of a red dragon to appear and breathe fire with the strength of an adult red dragon. In addition to the enormous 20d10 fireball, the force of the dragon's breath knocks an opponent off their feet and away from the caster. The victim can save vs. Breath Weapon to take half damage and not be blown backwards. Magic Resistance cannot block the effects of this spell. 

This spell will not harm party members.~

@6243 = ~Larloch's Interrupter (Necromantic)
Level: 5
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: special
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: One creature
Saving Throw: None

With this spell, the wizard manipulates the life force of a target to disturb the target's concentration as well as causing some damage. Once the spell hits the target, it inflicts 1D6 magic damage; after a second it inflicts 1D6 additional damage, and one second later, it causes one final shock which does another 1D6 magic damage. The spell cannot interrupt the target's use of items and scrolls. Magic Resistance cannot block the effects of this spell.~

@6244 = ~Improved Alacrity
(Any School)

Level: 10
Range: 0
Duration: 2 rounds
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Improved Alacrity essentially erases the pause between casting spells. When cast, the wizard can begin casting a new spell the instant <PRO_HESHE> is finished casting <PRO_HISHER> current spell. The effect lasts for 2 rounds and cannot be dispelled by any means.~

@6245 = ~Aura Cleansing
Level: 7
Range: Unlimited
Duration: 2 Rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: Special

Aura Cleansing essentially erases the pause between casting spells. When cast, the druid can begin casting a new spell the instant casting of the current spell is finished.  The effect lasts for 2 rounds and cannot be dispelled by any means.~

@6246 = ~Spellstrike (Abjuration)
Level: 9
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: Target Creature
Saving Throw: None

When this spell is cast at a target creature, it strips away all of the target's magic resistance, even if that creature is immune all other effects that would lower its magic resistance. Additionally, the target's resistances to fire, cold, electricity, acid and magic damage are lowered by 10%, unless the creature is completely immune to that damage type (i.e., has resistance of 100% or higher). Creatures immune to spells of level 9, or protected by Spell Immunity: Abjuration are still unaffected by this spell. This effect will last for 5 rounds or till 5 hostile attacks are performed against the target, be it a hit from a weapon, or a spell applying damage or negative effects. The effects of this spell are not cumulative. The target's magic resistance, if any, does not affect this spell.~

@6247 = ~Spellstrike effect ended.~

@6248 = ~Bigby's Clenched Fist (Evocation)
Level: 8
Range: Visual range of caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell creates a giant disembodied hand to squeeze and constrict the target. Upon being cast, the spell immediately inflicts 8D6 crushing damage with no saving throw, which bypasses Mirror Images due to its size. The target's magic resistance (if any) cannot block the spell's effect.~

@6249 = ~Bigby's Crushing Hand (Evocation)
Level: 9
Range: Visual range of caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

This spell creates a huge disembodied fist that crushes the target. Upon being cast, the spell immediately inflicts 8D10 crushing damage with no saving throw, which bypasses Mirror Images due to its size. The target's magic resistance (if any) cannot block the spell's effect.~

@6250 = ~Fist of Nature
Level: Quest
Sphere: Combat, Summoning
Range: Visual range of caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: One Creature
Saving Throw: None

By means of this powerful spell, the druid uses his connection with nature to creates a huge disembodied fist that inflicts 6D10 crushing damage to the target. This spell not only affects the Rakshasa (who are otherwise immune to druidic spells), but even inflicts quadruple damage to them.~

@6251 = ~Black Blade of Disaster
(Evocation)

Level: 9
Range: 0
Duration: 18 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

This spell enables the caster to create a black, blade-shaped planar rift about three feet long. It jumps into the caster's hand and is used as a normal sword, remaining there for the duration of the spell. The caster is considered to be proficient to the point of Grand Mastery in this weapon. The sword acts as a +5 weapon and deals 4-24 damage to its victims. There is also a 10% chance with every hit that the sword drains 2 levels from the target and heals the wielder 20 Hit Points.~

@6252 = ~Deathblow
Activating this ability causes all physical attacks made by the warrior to instantly kill any creature that has fewer than 20 Hit Points at the time of the strike.
The effect is considered non-magical and thus bypasses most magical immunities to death effects, such as Death Ward or Spell Immunity: Necromancy. Creatures completely immune to physical damage, or those protected by Stoneskins are immune to the effect.

 The effect lasts for 2 rounds and cannot be dispelled by any means.~

@6253 = ~Greater Deathblow
Activating this ability causes all physical attacks made by the warrior to instantly kill any creature that has fewer than 30 Hit Points at the time of the strike.
The effect is considered non-magical and thus bypasses magical immunities to death effects, such as Death Ward, Spell Immunity: Necromancy, or Protection from Death Magic. Creatures completely immune to physical damage, or those protected by Stoneskins are immune to the effect.

The effect lasts for 3 rounds and cannot be dispelled by any means.

Requires: Deathblow~

@6254 = ~Dexterous Retreat~

@6255 = ~Spell Turning (Abjuration)
Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 15 rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

This powerful abjuration spell causes the spells cast against the wizard to rebound upon the original caster. This effects a total of 12 spell levels for spells from level 1 to 9, for example 4 3rd-level, or 1 6th and 1 7th-level, etc.. This includes spells cast from scrolls and innate spell-like abilities, but excludes the following: spells removing spell protections like Secret Word or Ruby Ray of Reversal, Breach, Lower Resistance, instant area effects like Fireball, as well as area effects that are stationary such as cloud kill and stinking cloud. As long as the spell is cast directly at the wizard it will be reflected back upon the caster. Something to note is that as long as there are levels remaining then the spell will be reflected. For example if there is only 1 level left and a 3rd-level spell is cast at the wizard, the spell will be reflected while cancelling the spell turning. This spell will not protect the caster from dispel magic. However it will not be affected by dispel magic either.~

@6256 = ~Psionic Barrier~

@6257 = ~Telekinetic Pull~

@6258 = ~Split Mind~

@6259 = ~Casting speed decreased by 5~

@6260 = ~Casting speed decreased by 4~

@6261 = ~Casting speed decreased by 3~

@6262 = ~Casting speed decreased by 2~

@6263 = ~Casting speed decreased by 1~

@6264 = ~Heal
(Necromancy)

Level: 6
Sphere: Healing 
Range: Touch
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

The very potent Heal spell enables the priest to wipe away disease and injury in the creature who receives the benefits of the spell. It completely cures all disease and blindness in the recipient and heals all points of damage suffered due to wounds or injury and removes casting speed penalties caused by damage done to vocal cords by spells like Greater Silence, though it does not cure the silence effect itself. It also dispels a Feeblemind spell and cures those mental disorders caused by spells or injury to the brain. Naturally, the effects can be negated by later wounds, injuries, and diseases.~

@6265 = ~Mend Body
(Necromancy)

Level: 6
Sphere: Healing
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

Mend Body is the epitome of the shaman's ability to channel spiritual energy into the cure of physical trauma. This spell completely removes all disease and blindness in the recipient, recovers up to 60% of health lost due to wounds or injury and removes casting speed penalties caused by damage done to vocal cords by spells like Greater Silence, though it does not cure the silence effect itself. It also dispels a Feeblemind spell and cures those mental disorders caused by spells or injury to the brain. Naturally, the effects can be negated by later wounds, injuries, and diseases.~

@6266 = ~Sense of Limbo
(Alteration)

Level: 7
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

By casting this spell, the caster opens a short-lasting connection to the Ethereal Plane for the target, which can be used to cast magic by channeling the verbal part of the incantantion into the Prime Material Plane without the need to employ their vocal cords. Effectively, this allows the target to become immune to even the most debilitating forms of silence and removes all effects of such spells. Additionally this spell removes all forms of miscast magic and protects from that effect for its duration or until dispelled.~

@6267 = ~Animate Skeleton Grandlord~

@6268 = ~Drain Necrotic Energy~

@6269 = ~Dominate Undead~

@6270 = ~Energy Drain
(Necromancy)

Level: 9
Range: 15 ft.
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: None

The casting of this spell opens a channel between the caster's plane and the Negative Energy Plane. The caster of the spell acts as a conduit between the two planes, sucking life from a victim and transferring it to the Negative Energy Plane, draining <PRO_HIMHER> of 2 levels of experience and dealing 50 magic damage, which is transferred to the caster, healing him and increasing his maximum amount of health points (non-cumulative) for 3 turns. The target of this spell loses levels, Hit Dice, Hit Points, and abilities permanently. These levels can only be restored by a priest's Restoration spell. This spell does not work on creatures that don't have vital energy, like Undead, Golems or Elementals. The spell bypasses magic resistance of the target.~

@6271 = ~Casting abilities weakened~

@6272 = ~Physical resistances weakened~

@6273 = ~Curse of the Lich~

@6274 = ~Heavenly Shield

By casting this spell the Paladin imbues <PRO_HISHER> shield with divine magic, making it feel lighter in <PRO_HISHER> hand. This allows the caster to use the shield offensively, by searching for openings in enemy's defences and striking with the shield when the time is right. The better the caster's ability to fight using a shield, the greater the benefits of this spell.

Each first hit per round for the next turn deals additional crushing damage if the caster is using a shield. The base value is 2d3 plus additional 2d4 per each point in Sword and Shield style. Each strike is considered as highly magical, even with a non-magical shield, which allows for hitting creatures of magical nature, however spells like Protection from Magical Weapons can block the effects of this spell.~

@6275 = ~Aura of Courage~

@6276 = ~Absolute Immunity
(Abjuration) 

Level: 9
Range: 0
Duration: 4 rounds
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None 

When the spell is cast, it confers complete invulnerability to all weapons and increases physical resistances to 100%, thus making the caster immune to all sources of physical damage. This spell is incredibly powerful, hence the short duration. However, the casting time is also very short, making this spell incredibly useful in the thick of combat, where buying a few seconds can mean the difference between life or death. It is important to note that this spell does not work in combination with Protection From Magical Weapons. This spell lasts for the duration or until dispelled.~

@6277 = ~Guardian's Stand~

@6278 = ~Finish Guardian's Stand~

@6279 = ~Guardian's Stand

By planting their feet and raising their shield, the Cavalier creates a protective barrier against incoming fire and missiles. Through steady defense and trained reflexes, they deflect much of the harm aimed at those nearby.

While maintaining this stance, the Cavalier is immobile and unable to take other actions. All allies within 4 feet gain 50% resistance to fire and missile damage for up to 6 seconds, or until the Cavalier ends the stance early by using Finish Guardian's Stand.

A shield must be equipped for this ability to function. Once the stance ends, it cannot be used again for 1 second. This ability does not require the Cavalier's action to be free for this round and can be used immediately.

Both Guardian's Stand and Finish Guardian's Stand can be used instantly, even if the Cavalier's aura is not cleansed.~


@6281 = ~Plate Armor Mastery~

@6282 = ~Plate Armor Mastery

Mastery of the heaviest armors grants the Paladin +1 AC and +5% physical resistance while wearing plate or full plate.~

@6283 = ~Protection From Evil, 10' Radius 

When this spell is cast, all allied creatures within a 15-ft. radius are affected individually by Protection From Evil. It creates a magical barrier around the recipients at a distance of one foot. The barrier moves with the recipient and has two major effects: First, all attacks made by evil or evilly enchanted creatures against the protected creature receive a penalty of -2 to each attack roll. Second, summoned demons cannot target protected creatures. This effect lasts for 1 turn per Paladin level up to 20 turns.~

@6284 = ~Cleansing Light~

@6285 = ~Cleansing Light

The Cavalier calls upon divine strength to purge all effects that weaken resolve or cloud judgment, removing all effects of Doom, Greater Doom, Greater Malison and Aura of Malison and Field of Dark Magic from himself or one touched creature.~

@6286 = ~Shield Bash~

@6287 = ~Shield Bash~

@6288 = ~Shield Bash~

@6289 = ~Shield Bash~

